{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"title":"SkeletonModification2DCCDIK","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"class","roleHeading":"Class","externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot27SkeletonModification2DCCDIKC","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SkeletonModification2DCCDIK","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SkeletonModification2DCCDIK"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SkeletonModification2DCCDIK"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SkeletonModification2D"},{"text":" uses an algorithm called Cyclic Coordinate Descent Inverse Kinematics, or CCDIK, to manipulate a chain of bones in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Skeleton2D"},{"text":" so it reaches a defined target.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"CCDIK works by rotating a set of bones, typically called a “bone chain”, on a single axis. Each bone is rotated to face the target from the tip (by default), which over a chain of bones allow it to rotate properly to reach the target. Because the bones only rotate on a single axis, CCDIK ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"can"}]},{"text":" look more robotic than other IK solvers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The CCDIK modifier has "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ccdik_joints"},{"type":"text","text":", which are the data objects that hold the data for each joint in the CCDIK chain. This is different from a bone! CCDIK joints hold the data needed for each bone in the bone chain used by CCDIK."}]}],"type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CCDIK also fully supports angle constraints, allowing for more control over how a solution is met."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SkeletonModification2D"],"title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SQ","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SH","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s12IdentifiableP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/17SwiftGodotRuntime18VariantConvertibleP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SkeletonModification2DCCDIK","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A modification that uses CCDIK to manipulate a series of bones to reach a target in 2D."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SkeletonModification2DCCDIK\/ccdikDataChainLength","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SkeletonModification2DCCDIK\/targetNodepath","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SkeletonModification2DCCDIK\/tipNodepath"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SkeletonModification2DCCDIK\/getCcdikJointBone2dNode(jointIdx:)","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SkeletonModification2DCCDIK\/getCcdikJointBoneIndex(jointIdx:)","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SkeletonModification2DCCDIK\/getCcdikJointConstraintAngleInvert(jointIdx:)","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftG